 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and closed: no compatibility artifacts or aliases, bodies unexposed behind `(rfl)` `_def`/`_apply` lemmas, and all four private helpers are either the k=0 case of a public lemma (`sign_between`, `sign_order_aux`) or proof-internal glue, so none is general infrastructure in hiding. Both the Fin-indexed and \u2115-indexed comparison loops are usable without unfolding, and the simp/grind split matches Mathlib's `sign` API in `Mathlib/Basic/Sign/Defs.lean`.",
